<speak>
From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your daily briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">18022026</say-as>.
<break time="1s"/>
In politics.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Iran</emphasis> closed the Strait of Hormuz for live-fire drills as indirect nuclear talks continued in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʒəˈnɛvə">Geneva</phoneme>. The waterway carries <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">20</say-as> percent of global oil supply, and the closure's timing leaves open whether <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="tɛˈhɾɑːn">Tehran</phoneme> is signaling leverage or testing Washington's resolve.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Peru's</emphasis> Congress voted <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">75</say-as> to <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">24</say-as> to remove President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="xoˈse ˈxeɾi">Jose Jeri</phoneme> after security footage showed him meeting a Chinese contractor whose firms supply the state. The country's eighth president in eight years will be chosen by lawmakers, with a general election set for April.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Russia's</emphasis> lower house of parliament passed a bill giving the Federal Security Service authority to shut down the internet, mobile networks, and postal services. The legislation, approved by <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">393</say-as> lawmakers to <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">13</say-as>, passes next to the upper chamber and President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈputɪn">Putin</phoneme> for signature.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Canada</emphasis> announced more than five hundred billion dollars in defence and security investment. Prime Minister <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmɑːk ˈkɑːrni">Mark Carney</phoneme> framed the overhaul as an explicit break from reliance on United States suppliers, calling that dependency untenable under the Trump administration.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">South Korea's</emphasis> courts will rule Thursday on whether former President <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="jun sʌk jʌl">Yoon Suk-yeol</phoneme>'s <say-as interpret-as="date" format="y">2024</say-as> martial law decree constituted insurrection. Prosecutors have demanded the death penalty, and a conviction would permanently bar him from public office.
<break time="900ms"/>
In conflict and security.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Lebanon's</emphasis> <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈhɛzbəlɑː">Hezbollah</phoneme>-aligned ministers walked out of cabinet after the group's secretary-general rejected the government's four-month disarmament timeline. Without the movement's cooperation, the ceasefire covering weapons north of the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="liˈtɑːni">Litani</phoneme> River has no enforcement path.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">United States</emphasis> military strikes on alleged drug-trafficking boats have killed at least <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">145</say-as> people since September, with three more strikes adding <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">11</say-as> deaths this week. The United Nations human rights chief warned none of the targets posed an imminent threat justifying lethal force.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Russia</emphasis> and Ukraine held a second day of United States-mediated talks in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ʒəˈnɛvə">Geneva</phoneme>, ending after just two hours with territory still the central deadlock. Both sides confirmed more rounds will follow, though Russia launched missiles and drones at Ukraine the same day.
<break time="900ms"/>
On the economy.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Germany's</emphasis> <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈbaɪɐ">Bayer</phoneme> offered seven point two five billion dollars to settle one hundred thousand cancer claims linked to its Roundup weedkiller. The company has already paid eleven billion dollars in glyphosate litigation since acquiring <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈmɒnsæntoʊ">Monsanto</phoneme> in <say-as interpret-as="date" format="y">2018</say-as>, while the Supreme Court weighs a separate appeal to shield future lawsuits.
<break time="600ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">South Africa's</emphasis> <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ɛm tiː ɛn">MTN</phoneme> Group agreed to buy <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="aɪ eɪtʃ ɛs">IHS</phoneme> Towers for six point two billion dollars, gaining control of <say-as interpret-as="cardinal">29000</say-as> towers across five African countries. The deal represents the largest consolidation of mobile infrastructure on the continent in years.
<break time="900ms"/>
In science.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Antarctica</emphasis> has become the latest continent reached by the H5N1 bird flu strain. Migratory birds carried the virus nine hundred kilometres along the coastline, where it can kill an entire colony within days, leaving tens of thousands of penguins, cormorants, and seals at risk with no available treatment.
<break time="900ms"/>
In technology.<break time="400ms"/>
<emphasis level="strong">Tesla's</emphasis> autonomous robotaxis in <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="ˈɔːstɪn">Austin</phoneme> are crashing at four times the rate of human drivers. Fourteen collisions in eight months include one the company quietly reclassified to add a hospitalisation five months later, while no federal investigation has been opened.
<break time="1s"/>
That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.
</speak>